1
00:00:49,049 --> 00:00:52,219
THE ORDINARY JACKPOT

2
00:01:02,688 --> 00:01:04,940
SHIPPING COST

3
00:01:23,792 --> 00:01:24,793
Good morning.

4
00:01:32,259 --> 00:01:34,803
- Hello, Mr. Gong.
- Morning, Ms. Jang.

5
00:01:44,229 --> 00:01:45,480
When did you get to work?

6
00:01:46,189 --> 00:01:48,150
I got to the café an hour ago.

7
00:01:49,401 --> 00:01:51,361
I came in an hour
and ten minutes ago.

8
00:01:52,613 --> 00:01:53,988
Why did you come so early?

9
00:01:53,989 --> 00:01:55,072
What about you?

10
00:01:55,073 --> 00:01:56,366
I asked you first.

11
00:01:56,617 --> 00:01:58,409
I don't want to answer first.

12
00:01:58,410 --> 00:02:00,037
That's why I asked you first.

13
00:02:03,123 --> 00:02:04,499
I do this when I'm nervous.

14
00:02:06,251 --> 00:02:07,419
I work harder

15
00:02:08,045 --> 00:02:09,670
get things ready faster

16
00:02:09,671 --> 00:02:11,423
try to sleep less

17
00:02:12,007 --> 00:02:14,051
and even run simulations in my head.

18
00:02:16,970 --> 00:02:18,138
It's your turn now.

19
00:02:20,891 --> 00:02:22,351
I miscalculated the time.

20
00:02:23,644 --> 00:02:27,105
I meant to get here a little early,
but I came too early.

21
00:02:30,776 --> 00:02:33,862
Aren't I pathetic,
how I'm always tense and nervous?

22
00:02:35,280 --> 00:02:36,281
Not at all.

23
00:02:36,740 --> 00:02:39,201
I think that's why
you're good at what you do.

24
00:02:39,701 --> 00:02:40,911
You don't make mistakes.

25
00:02:41,328 --> 00:02:43,747
Me? I make a ton of mistakes.

26
00:02:44,164 --> 00:02:45,165
Do you?

27
00:02:45,916 --> 00:02:48,126
Nothing ever goes the way I plan.

28
00:02:48,627 --> 00:02:49,878
I make loads of mistakes.

29
00:02:51,672 --> 00:02:52,964
But if you practice hard enough

30
00:02:54,257 --> 00:02:56,009
you can make up for the mistakes.

31
00:02:58,929 --> 00:03:00,931
Let's go. Time to make some mistakes.

32
00:03:14,611 --> 00:03:19,157
EPISODE 7:
NOTHING HAS CHANGED

33
00:03:21,076 --> 00:03:22,285
SALES DIVISION 2
EXPORT SALES CONTRACT

34
00:03:30,502 --> 00:03:31,586
Mr. Choi.

35
00:03:32,796 --> 00:03:36,048
I asked for all documents produced
or received by Sales Division 2

36
00:03:36,049 --> 00:03:37,800
in the last two years,
separated by team.

37
00:03:37,801 --> 00:03:39,302
Is this everything?

38
00:03:40,053 --> 00:03:42,638
It's all here, as you asked.

39
00:03:42,639 --> 00:03:46,058
We will penalize you
if we find anything missing.

40
00:03:46,059 --> 00:03:48,186
I'm sure you will. I know that.

41
00:03:48,687 --> 00:03:50,021
I hope that never happens.

42
00:03:57,946 --> 00:03:59,573
AUDIT IN PROGRESS
AUTHORIZED PERSONNEL ONLY

43
00:04:12,586 --> 00:04:14,546
Do we have to go through all that?

44
00:04:21,970 --> 00:04:24,138
- Hi, Ji-hye.
- Enjoy your meal.

45
00:04:24,139 --> 00:04:25,807
- Enjoy.
- You too.

46
00:04:26,433 --> 00:04:28,852
Do you think Mr. Gong
and Ms. Jang ate lunch?

47
00:04:29,895 --> 00:04:33,315
They'll eat something way nicer.
Why would you worry?

48
00:04:34,191 --> 00:04:35,192
Mr. Yang.

49
00:04:35,734 --> 00:04:36,985
What will happen to Division 2?

50
00:04:37,360 --> 00:04:39,321
All we have so far is a tip-off.

51
00:04:39,780 --> 00:04:41,072
They might find nothing.

52
00:04:41,448 --> 00:04:43,366
I don't know much about this

53
00:04:44,117 --> 00:04:46,119
but I hope they don't find anything.

54
00:04:46,703 --> 00:04:48,871
Do you think that's the best outcome?

55
00:04:48,872 --> 00:04:49,955
Of course.

56
00:04:49,956 --> 00:04:54,503
We're all family here.
I hope no one has to suffer.

57
00:04:55,253 --> 00:04:56,755
Why would no one suffer?

58
00:04:57,214 --> 00:05:00,175
If they find nothing,
Mr. Gong and Ms. Jang suffer.

59
00:05:01,009 --> 00:05:03,677
Oh, is that how it works?

60
00:05:03,678 --> 00:05:06,597
When it's about work,
there's no such thing as nothing.

61
00:05:06,598 --> 00:05:08,225
There must always be a result.

62
00:05:08,683 --> 00:05:11,853
The only difference is whether
it's a scratch or a grave injury.

63
00:05:13,230 --> 00:05:17,484
Then we should hope
they find something.

64
00:05:17,901 --> 00:05:19,319
My personal wish is

65
00:05:20,195 --> 00:05:22,447
that they find a small mistake
that results in a scratch.

66
00:05:23,073 --> 00:05:25,700
Best-case scenario,
everyone gets off with a scratch.

67
00:05:26,618 --> 00:05:28,745
Is there anything
we could do to help?

68
00:05:29,454 --> 00:05:31,206
In that case, Ji-hye...

69
00:05:32,415 --> 00:05:35,292
Pray and hope the heavens help us.

70
00:05:35,293 --> 00:05:36,670
So they return unscathed.

71
00:05:37,295 --> 00:05:38,296
Okay.

72
00:05:40,674 --> 00:05:42,925
I love that you cut up
the pork cutlet.

73
00:05:42,926 --> 00:05:45,470
Wait, you said you didn't want any.

74
00:05:49,057 --> 00:05:50,058
Mr. Lee Jong-hyun.

75
00:05:51,017 --> 00:05:53,311
You've done business with us
for seven years.

76
00:05:53,687 --> 00:05:54,688
Yes.

77
00:05:54,980 --> 00:05:57,607
Considering the circumstances,
I'll get to the point.

78
00:05:58,149 --> 00:06:00,235
Sure. That would benefit everyone.

79
00:06:03,280 --> 00:06:06,490
I checked the details of the contract
you signed with us.

80
00:06:06,491 --> 00:06:08,577
It says the margin is 70%.

81
00:06:09,119 --> 00:06:11,580
Given the brand's recognition
and influence overseas

82
00:06:12,038 --> 00:06:14,374
it's a much better offer than usual.

83
00:06:15,125 --> 00:06:17,252
Can you describe
how the negotiations went?

84
00:06:17,836 --> 00:06:19,004
Hang on.

85
00:06:20,422 --> 00:06:21,715
Isn't the margin way too low?

86
00:06:23,049 --> 00:06:26,760
It is. It's almost the same
as what we get.

87
00:06:26,761 --> 00:06:29,431
Division 1 imports foreign brands

88
00:06:29,723 --> 00:06:31,640
and Division 2
exports domestic brands

89
00:06:31,641 --> 00:06:33,602
and yet the margin is
almost the same?

90
00:06:34,352 --> 00:06:36,770
Domestic brands aren't
that well-known overseas.

91
00:06:36,771 --> 00:06:38,981
Shouldn't Division 2
get a bigger margin?

92
00:06:38,982 --> 00:06:40,692
There could be a side agreement.

93
00:06:41,151 --> 00:06:44,696
The contract says 70%,
but in reality, they get 75%.

94
00:06:45,196 --> 00:06:47,824
And someone pockets
the 5% difference.

95
00:06:52,996 --> 00:06:55,623
Our brand has weakened since

96
00:06:55,624 --> 00:06:59,085
but we once hit 50 billion won
in sales with a single brand.

97
00:06:59,794 --> 00:07:02,339
Our brand awareness
in Asia is improving.

98
00:07:04,466 --> 00:07:06,343
I don't think we're taking too much.

99
00:07:07,802 --> 00:07:09,638
Did you bring the contract?

100
00:07:10,096 --> 00:07:11,514
I believe we asked you to.

101
00:07:16,811 --> 00:07:17,854
Here you go.

102
00:07:18,855 --> 00:07:20,606
He won't admit to it.

103
00:07:20,607 --> 00:07:23,442
Their contract will say
the same as ours.

104
00:07:23,443 --> 00:07:25,612
There's no issue with the contract.

105
00:07:26,696 --> 00:07:30,325
We can't find anything
unless we check their accounts.

106
00:07:30,825 --> 00:07:33,244
You won't get anything
from the accounts, either.

107
00:07:33,620 --> 00:07:36,706
They made it so business expenses
don't require receipts.

108
00:07:37,040 --> 00:07:38,458
They'd have paid in cash.

109
00:07:39,167 --> 00:07:41,628
How about pressuring them
by saying we'll file a complaint?

110
00:07:44,714 --> 00:07:45,715
Mr. Lee.

111
00:07:46,299 --> 00:07:49,803
We suspect you paid kickbacks
under the table.

112
00:07:51,596 --> 00:07:53,056
That's nonsense.

113
00:07:54,099 --> 00:07:55,475
There were no kickbacks.

114
00:07:56,559 --> 00:07:59,562
Admit to it now,
and it'll be kept between us.

115
00:08:00,188 --> 00:08:03,984
We can penalize our personnel,
and you can handle yours.

116
00:08:04,776 --> 00:08:06,277
However, if you don't admit to it

117
00:08:06,987 --> 00:08:08,738
we have no choice
but to involve prosecution.

118
00:08:09,948 --> 00:08:11,950
Do you have any proof
to warrant that?

119
00:08:13,034 --> 00:08:16,705
Would a prosecutor investigate
on suspicion only, without proof?

120
00:08:16,955 --> 00:08:18,248
There's circumstantial evidence.

121
00:08:18,707 --> 00:08:21,626
Some of our staff have a conscience,
and they blew a whistle.

122
00:08:24,004 --> 00:08:25,338
File a complaint
and have them investigate.

123
00:08:27,382 --> 00:08:30,677
But if they don't find anything

124
00:08:31,261 --> 00:08:33,221
I will hold Hongsung responsible.

125
00:08:34,347 --> 00:08:35,348
How?

126
00:08:36,850 --> 00:08:38,518
How will you hold us responsible?

127
00:08:40,687 --> 00:08:43,106
Do you think we're incapable
of taking action?

128
00:08:43,815 --> 00:08:46,818
Is that why you're saying
you'll do something

129
00:08:47,610 --> 00:08:49,612
when you can't really do anything?

130
00:08:50,822 --> 00:08:52,949
You've gone a little too far.

131
00:08:53,783 --> 00:08:55,910
Is this the price I pay
for doing business with Hongsung?

132
00:08:56,494 --> 00:08:58,872
You can't treat me
like a common criminal.

133
00:08:59,998 --> 00:09:04,294
They wouldn't have come this far
if a warning worked at all.

134
00:09:04,711 --> 00:09:07,881
True. They'd be well-prepared.

135
00:09:08,214 --> 00:09:09,924
This is as far as an audit can go.

136
00:09:10,425 --> 00:09:14,137
We can't check personal accounts
or search another company's office.

137
00:09:16,306 --> 00:09:17,682
I really hate it

138
00:09:18,516 --> 00:09:19,642
but in this situation

139
00:09:19,976 --> 00:09:22,187
the only thing we can do
is give a warning.

140
00:09:22,645 --> 00:09:25,398
"We know what you did,
but we'll let you off this time."

141
00:09:26,066 --> 00:09:28,109
That alone works sometimes.

142
00:09:28,443 --> 00:09:30,070
Most people decide to play it safe.

143
00:09:31,738 --> 00:09:33,655
We can't do that this time.

144
00:09:33,656 --> 00:09:37,077
The VP ordered this audit,
and the whole board is involved.

145
00:09:38,203 --> 00:09:40,246
We must bring them something.

146
00:09:40,914 --> 00:09:42,540
Then find me something.

147
00:09:42,916 --> 00:09:45,126
All I know is the law,
and it looks fine to me.

148
00:09:49,506 --> 00:09:50,757
This is definitely odd.

149
00:09:52,926 --> 00:09:54,344
My experience tells me to focus

150
00:09:54,636 --> 00:09:56,554
on money going out
rather than money coming in.

151
00:09:57,680 --> 00:09:59,182
SHIPPING COST
BRICLOGIX

152
00:10:05,605 --> 00:10:08,358
Can I ask why Hongsung
covered the shipping costs?

153
00:10:11,778 --> 00:10:14,072
That depends on the agreement.

154
00:10:14,489 --> 00:10:15,490
No.

155
00:10:16,032 --> 00:10:20,453
Shipping costs are never covered
by the brand controller.

156
00:10:20,912 --> 00:10:22,579
That's included in the margin.

157
00:10:22,580 --> 00:10:24,415
That might never happen elsewhere

158
00:10:24,999 --> 00:10:26,084
but we agreed to it.

159
00:10:26,709 --> 00:10:28,670
That's how considerate Mr. Choi is.

160
00:10:29,420 --> 00:10:31,421
Ask him about it.

161
00:10:31,422 --> 00:10:32,549
We already did.

162
00:10:35,927 --> 00:10:37,595
That's the shipping company's
bank statement.

163
00:10:38,429 --> 00:10:40,890
It's a sole proprietorship,
so it conducts transactions freely.

164
00:10:41,641 --> 00:10:43,017
The owner already confessed

165
00:10:43,643 --> 00:10:46,271
to receiving payments
from both companies

166
00:10:46,563 --> 00:10:49,065
laundering them as salaries,
and returning the money to you.

167
00:10:52,026 --> 00:10:53,695
This is what I think happened.

168
00:10:54,863 --> 00:10:56,488
You kept getting off with warnings

169
00:10:56,489 --> 00:10:58,158
and no one actually did anything.

170
00:10:58,616 --> 00:10:59,951
So you got more brazen.

171
00:11:01,953 --> 00:11:02,996
You and us both.

172
00:11:08,501 --> 00:11:10,253
Will you admit to it now?

173
00:11:17,260 --> 00:11:18,261
Jeez.

174
00:11:20,054 --> 00:11:22,140
You should've said from the start
that you knew everything.

175
00:11:23,600 --> 00:11:25,560
Why did you make me lie?

176
00:11:27,604 --> 00:11:28,605
We gave you a chance.

177
00:11:30,231 --> 00:11:31,858
And you just lost it.

178
00:11:42,285 --> 00:11:45,205
You should've said
it was a fucking chance.

179
00:12:00,762 --> 00:12:02,305
How much is the shipping cost?

180
00:12:08,436 --> 00:12:10,855
It's 2% of the total invoiced amount.

181
00:12:11,231 --> 00:12:13,316
You took it, but instead
of keeping it all to yourself

182
00:12:14,400 --> 00:12:16,069
you gave some of it to the brand?

183
00:12:18,404 --> 00:12:19,405
I'm asking you.

184
00:12:21,324 --> 00:12:22,325
I'm sorry, sir.

185
00:12:23,660 --> 00:12:26,496
He got a kickback from a kickback.

186
00:12:27,830 --> 00:12:29,958
He knew you were taking
from the company

187
00:12:30,333 --> 00:12:32,752
so he asked you
for a piece of the pie.

188
00:12:33,878 --> 00:12:36,506
What did they take us for,
making a demand like that?

189
00:12:37,465 --> 00:12:38,466
I'm sorry, sir.

190
00:12:40,927 --> 00:12:42,095
What are you sorry about?

191
00:12:43,388 --> 00:12:45,223
You wouldn't have done this
if you felt bad.

192
00:12:46,683 --> 00:12:47,684
Mr. Gong.

193
00:12:48,393 --> 00:12:49,394
Yes, sir.

194
00:12:50,645 --> 00:12:53,189
Apart from the shipping costs,
you suspect a side agreement?

195
00:12:53,648 --> 00:12:56,149
Yes, the brand margin
was excessively high.

196
00:12:56,150 --> 00:12:58,528
VICE PRESIDENT KOO IN-MOCK

197
00:13:00,738 --> 00:13:01,739
Mr. Choi.

198
00:13:02,949 --> 00:13:04,075
Yes, sir.

199
00:13:05,451 --> 00:13:07,203
How about you admit to what you did

200
00:13:08,121 --> 00:13:09,998
cough up as much of the money you can

201
00:13:11,416 --> 00:13:12,917
and leave voluntarily?

202
00:13:18,673 --> 00:13:20,091
Do you need time to think?

203
00:13:21,301 --> 00:13:23,011
No, sir.

204
00:13:25,471 --> 00:13:28,433
I'll cooperate with the Audit Team.

205
00:13:31,978 --> 00:13:33,813
- Yoon.
- Yes, sir.

206
00:13:34,689 --> 00:13:36,649
Aren't you
the youngest associate director?

207
00:13:37,191 --> 00:13:38,568
Yes, I am.

208
00:13:39,152 --> 00:13:41,112
You might also have
the shortest tenure ever.

209
00:13:44,073 --> 00:13:45,575
This is why

210
00:13:45,992 --> 00:13:48,076
you should never be proud
of an early promotion

211
00:13:48,077 --> 00:13:50,872
or despair that things
are taking too long for you.

212
00:13:51,748 --> 00:13:53,333
This is what people are like.

213
00:13:54,667 --> 00:13:57,086
Some rise fast only to fall fast.

214
00:13:58,504 --> 00:14:01,632
I have nothing more
to say about that.

215
00:14:07,513 --> 00:14:08,514
Ms. Park.

216
00:14:09,098 --> 00:14:10,099
Yes, sir.

217
00:14:10,516 --> 00:14:12,727
Handle Division 2 as well
for a while.

218
00:14:16,522 --> 00:14:17,523
Any issues with that?

219
00:14:18,274 --> 00:14:19,275
No, sir.

220
00:14:58,022 --> 00:14:59,107
You can go ahead.

221
00:15:10,743 --> 00:15:12,078
HOT MILK COFFEE
600 WON

222
00:15:19,794 --> 00:15:20,795
Thank you.

223
00:15:27,093 --> 00:15:28,428
I haven't been here in a while.

224
00:15:29,053 --> 00:15:30,721
We used to sit out here often.

225
00:15:31,722 --> 00:15:35,143
Our presence makes
other employees uncomfortable.

226
00:15:36,727 --> 00:15:38,104
Exactly.

227
00:15:38,729 --> 00:15:41,731
Is it the title or the age?

228
00:15:41,732 --> 00:15:43,651
Everyone complains about us.

229
00:15:46,821 --> 00:15:48,072
What will you do next?

230
00:15:50,199 --> 00:15:51,284
I don't know.

231
00:15:51,909 --> 00:15:54,036
I'm too afraid to do my own thing

232
00:15:54,912 --> 00:15:56,873
so I'd like to find a decent opening.

233
00:15:57,373 --> 00:16:00,877
But I doubt anyone would want
a troublemaker like me.

234
00:16:01,878 --> 00:16:03,379
It's too late for regret.

235
00:16:04,839 --> 00:16:06,090
Sorry about that.

236
00:16:08,176 --> 00:16:09,260
I get it, though.

237
00:16:10,178 --> 00:16:12,346
I think I might have done the same.

238
00:16:13,931 --> 00:16:16,809
A uselessly lofty title
means more expenses.

239
00:16:17,226 --> 00:16:19,896
People are watching, so you
have to be seen at decent places

240
00:16:20,438 --> 00:16:22,565
but not places that are too fancy.

241
00:16:23,858 --> 00:16:27,069
Others with our titles own
a nice place and a nice car

242
00:16:28,446 --> 00:16:30,698
yet you're still struggling
to pay off a mortgage.

243
00:16:31,282 --> 00:16:33,409
That's when you start to want more.

244
00:16:34,744 --> 00:16:37,330
It doesn't help
that others embezzle too.

245
00:16:38,247 --> 00:16:40,750
It feels like staying honest
means falling behind.

246
00:16:41,375 --> 00:16:45,713
It starts off by accepting
a kickback you're offered.

247
00:16:46,088 --> 00:16:48,549
Then you end up stealing
the shipping costs.

248
00:16:51,135 --> 00:16:53,554
It doesn't take much to become lousy.

249
00:16:54,305 --> 00:16:56,807
Even people like you,
who were once so decent.

250
00:16:57,934 --> 00:16:59,519
I have no excuses.

251
00:17:00,853 --> 00:17:02,021
Don't say that.

252
00:17:02,730 --> 00:17:05,440
I didn't bring you out here
to lecture you.

253
00:17:05,441 --> 00:17:08,486
No, I should've been...

254
00:17:09,570 --> 00:17:11,531
I should've been lectured.

255
00:17:12,698 --> 00:17:15,076
If I'd remained under you...

256
00:17:18,829 --> 00:17:20,331
this wouldn't have happened.

257
00:17:23,626 --> 00:17:26,254
Being a parent
whose child committed a crime.

258
00:17:27,171 --> 00:17:28,422
Do you know that feeling?

259
00:17:29,632 --> 00:17:31,759
The child must pay for what they did.

260
00:17:34,387 --> 00:17:35,930
But despite what they did

261
00:17:37,473 --> 00:17:40,184
you still love your child.

262
00:17:43,020 --> 00:17:45,481
You wonder
if you failed them somehow.

263
00:17:47,817 --> 00:17:50,027
- That's it.
- I'm so sorry.

264
00:17:52,697 --> 00:17:53,698
I just...

265
00:17:55,283 --> 00:17:56,367
I just wanted to have

266
00:17:57,326 --> 00:17:59,787
a coffee out here with you
like the old times.

267
00:18:03,624 --> 00:18:05,376
Tell me when you decide what to do.

268
00:18:06,419 --> 00:18:07,878
And if you need help.

269
00:18:08,462 --> 00:18:09,463
I will.

270
00:18:11,132 --> 00:18:12,466
Thank you, Ms. Park.

271
00:18:13,551 --> 00:18:14,635
Thank you.

272
00:18:25,730 --> 00:18:27,523
- Mr. Gong.
- Yes?

273
00:18:28,482 --> 00:18:30,526
How did it go?
I haven't heard anything.

274
00:18:32,278 --> 00:18:34,155
The Audit Team
will be wrapping it up.

275
00:18:38,701 --> 00:18:40,036
Did you see the holiday gift?

276
00:18:44,040 --> 00:18:46,459
But they left her out again...

277
00:18:47,209 --> 00:18:48,461
Sorry to interrupt, Mr. Gong.

278
00:18:48,961 --> 00:18:50,463
No, go ahead.

279
00:18:51,505 --> 00:18:52,840
Did you check my proposal?

280
00:18:53,507 --> 00:18:54,508
Yes, I did.

281
00:18:55,301 --> 00:18:58,136
The son of the mall's VP
is getting married this weekend?

282
00:18:58,137 --> 00:19:00,473
Yes, we sent a flower arrangement
in Hongsung's name.

283
00:19:00,931 --> 00:19:02,266
Who paid for it?

284
00:19:03,059 --> 00:19:05,685
We put it on your card.

285
00:19:05,686 --> 00:19:08,021
You should've put it
on the director's card.

286
00:19:08,022 --> 00:19:10,940
She told us to put it on yours.

287
00:19:10,941 --> 00:19:12,234
Darn it.

288
00:19:14,403 --> 00:19:15,863
What is it this time?

289
00:19:19,617 --> 00:19:22,578
There's something we must sort out
before the holiday.

290
00:19:24,163 --> 00:19:25,289
Let's do it now.

291
00:19:31,128 --> 00:19:33,839
- What is this?
- An idea Team 4 came up with.

292
00:19:34,715 --> 00:19:35,716
Team 4?

293
00:19:36,967 --> 00:19:38,302
How are things over there?

294
00:19:39,553 --> 00:19:43,516
Mr. Oh is struggling
with the workload without a superior.

295
00:19:45,142 --> 00:19:46,851
Let's do it one at a time.

296
00:19:46,852 --> 00:19:48,436
Don't you see the mess I'm in?

297
00:19:48,437 --> 00:19:51,691
I'm figuring out Division 2
on top of my usual workload.

298
00:19:57,905 --> 00:19:59,448
They want to work for a commission?

299
00:20:00,074 --> 00:20:02,242
The profit is low,
but so is the risk.

300
00:20:02,243 --> 00:20:04,745
I thought it could be
a decent long-term project.

301
00:20:05,871 --> 00:20:08,040
- Mr. Oh brought this to you?
- Yes.

302
00:20:09,583 --> 00:20:10,626
Was it his idea?

303
00:20:11,627 --> 00:20:13,421
I'm not sure about that.

304
00:20:14,088 --> 00:20:15,339
Get him in here.

305
00:20:18,843 --> 00:20:20,885
Come and sit next to him.

306
00:20:20,886 --> 00:20:22,054
- Hello, sir.
- Hi.

307
00:20:25,599 --> 00:20:28,519
Did you come up with this
on your own?

308
00:20:29,437 --> 00:20:32,689
It was Mr. Jeong's idea,
but I came up with all the details.

309
00:20:32,690 --> 00:20:34,692
He said it would be
a good first project.

310
00:20:36,777 --> 00:20:40,823
I can tell how much you've put
into your first project.

311
00:20:41,615 --> 00:20:42,783
It's like my own baby.

312
00:20:44,869 --> 00:20:45,995
Oh, dear...

313
00:20:47,496 --> 00:20:50,416
Jeong was way worse than I thought.

314
00:20:56,172 --> 00:20:59,800
A non-profit business
isn't just for anyone.

315
00:21:00,676 --> 00:21:02,887
First, we must survive
until we turn a profit.

316
00:21:03,888 --> 00:21:05,305
Even when the industry is booming

317
00:21:05,306 --> 00:21:08,142
no one would rely
on a single non-profit business.

318
00:21:09,435 --> 00:21:11,562
See if they're doing business
with Jeong's company.

319
00:21:12,271 --> 00:21:15,316
I bet they signed the real business
with a huge margin.

320
00:21:15,983 --> 00:21:19,403
We do all the hard work
while Jeong takes all the profit.

321
00:21:21,280 --> 00:21:22,865
Do you get what I'm saying, Mr. Oh?

322
00:21:24,033 --> 00:21:25,034
Yes.

323
00:21:27,953 --> 00:21:29,955
You made a decent dish,
but the ingredients were rotten.

324
00:21:30,414 --> 00:21:31,957
Bring me something else.

325
00:21:32,500 --> 00:21:34,627
I liked the details,
so don't blame yourself.

326
00:21:35,586 --> 00:21:37,463
Yes, sir. Thank you.

327
00:21:38,005 --> 00:21:40,257
You can go. Gong, you stay.

328
00:21:53,979 --> 00:21:56,106
Do you know how humiliating that is?

329
00:21:57,274 --> 00:22:00,528
If we approve this
after demolishing a whole division

330
00:22:00,778 --> 00:22:02,822
they'll call us
honest but incompetent.

331
00:22:04,490 --> 00:22:07,784
Do you want them to say
they'd rather hire

332
00:22:07,785 --> 00:22:09,078
a competent but dishonest man?

333
00:22:13,958 --> 00:22:15,334
Eun-tae.

334
00:22:15,668 --> 00:22:18,003
You really worry me sometimes.

335
00:22:20,256 --> 00:22:23,175
Have you ever driven a nice car?

336
00:22:24,802 --> 00:22:27,763
- Pardon?
- You know, an expensive, fast car.

337
00:22:29,181 --> 00:22:31,767
I once got to sit
in the passenger seat.

338
00:22:32,601 --> 00:22:34,770
Didn't you feel uneasy?

339
00:22:36,647 --> 00:22:39,149
When a bad driver handles a fancy car

340
00:22:39,733 --> 00:22:41,777
it's the passenger who suffers.

341
00:22:45,781 --> 00:22:47,283
Your car is way too fancy.

342
00:22:47,908 --> 00:22:49,076
Watch how you drive it.

343
00:23:46,175 --> 00:23:48,010
- I don't think it looks right.
- Really?

344
00:23:48,802 --> 00:23:51,472
The brighter color might work
since it's women's wear.

345
00:23:52,932 --> 00:23:54,308
Yes, but the current trend...

346
00:23:54,642 --> 00:23:55,768
But still...

347
00:23:56,435 --> 00:23:57,978
What about the other colors?

348
00:23:58,395 --> 00:24:00,731
- Something brighter.
- Brighter?

349
00:24:01,148 --> 00:24:03,233
- Isn't this too bright?
- Are you all staying late?

350
00:24:03,943 --> 00:24:06,570
We have some stuff to wrap up.

351
00:24:06,987 --> 00:24:08,197
It must be done before the holiday.

352
00:24:08,697 --> 00:24:10,157
Finish it up and go home.

353
00:24:10,783 --> 00:24:11,825
I'm heading out.

354
00:24:12,826 --> 00:24:13,994
Bye, Mr. Gong.

355
00:24:14,328 --> 00:24:16,246
- Goodbye.
- Enjoy the holiday break.

356
00:24:31,345 --> 00:24:32,346
Mr. Gong!

357
00:24:36,850 --> 00:24:38,477
You left this behind.

358
00:24:42,272 --> 00:24:45,109
I gave it to you. Take it home.

359
00:24:46,568 --> 00:24:48,988
No, sir. It's fine.

360
00:24:50,239 --> 00:24:51,615
I want you to have it.

361
00:24:54,326 --> 00:24:55,327
Mr. Gong.

362
00:24:57,037 --> 00:24:58,539
You don't have to do this.

363
00:24:59,206 --> 00:25:00,874
Please, just take the gift.

364
00:25:02,543 --> 00:25:03,585
Okay, then.

365
00:25:09,383 --> 00:25:13,053
I'm really grateful, but...

366
00:25:14,138 --> 00:25:17,516
When Gi-tae made that mistake,
his first concern was

367
00:25:18,267 --> 00:25:22,354
if it would cost me
a full-time position.

368
00:25:23,272 --> 00:25:26,233
No one cares if a contract worker
gets a holiday gift or not

369
00:25:26,859 --> 00:25:29,445
but you left this under my desk.

370
00:25:30,779 --> 00:25:33,032
I'm really grateful, but...

371
00:25:38,370 --> 00:25:40,122
The more you care...

372
00:25:44,084 --> 00:25:45,586
the more I feel
like a contract worker.

373
00:25:50,632 --> 00:25:52,676
I should get back to work now.

374
00:25:54,803 --> 00:25:56,221
Enjoy your holiday.

375
00:26:06,398 --> 00:26:07,441
It was a mistake.

376
00:26:09,401 --> 00:26:12,946
A mistake I can't make up,
no matter how hard I try.

377
00:26:20,621 --> 00:26:22,873
Today, I ruined
a few colleagues' livelihoods.

378
00:26:26,085 --> 00:26:28,295
They might have done wrong

379
00:26:29,630 --> 00:26:32,549
but I was the one to reveal it
and get them punished.

380
00:26:37,346 --> 00:26:39,515
My superior criticized me.

381
00:26:40,849 --> 00:26:43,685
The one thing an employee
must never hear.

382
00:26:45,437 --> 00:26:47,648
"It's better to be corrupt
than incompetent."

383
00:26:48,315 --> 00:26:49,524
That's what he said to me.

384
00:26:49,525 --> 00:26:50,943
VERNIA STUDIO
GLOBAL EXPANSION BUSINESS PLAN

385
00:27:06,583 --> 00:27:09,628
I offended a team member
in the name of consideration.

386
00:27:14,383 --> 00:27:16,677
I didn't give her the gift
for her sake.

387
00:27:17,553 --> 00:27:19,304
I did it for my own.

388
00:27:22,558 --> 00:27:24,684
- That was so good.
- I really enjoyed that.

389
00:27:24,685 --> 00:27:26,144
It's a famous place.

390
00:27:26,145 --> 00:27:28,187
It was incredible. Seriously.

391
00:27:28,188 --> 00:27:29,730
Down for another round?

392
00:27:29,731 --> 00:27:30,940
- Let's go somewhere.
- For real?

393
00:27:30,941 --> 00:27:32,484
- What should we eat?
- What do you want?

394
00:28:05,976 --> 00:28:07,019
Today

395
00:28:07,519 --> 00:28:11,732
as a colleague,
a subordinate, and a superior

396
00:28:12,357 --> 00:28:13,775
I accomplished nothing.

397
00:28:16,987 --> 00:28:18,864
I thought things were going well.

398
00:28:19,698 --> 00:28:23,493
I'm rich, so I no longer work
to earn a living.

399
00:28:23,911 --> 00:28:27,789
I don't work for the money,
so the work became clearer.

400
00:28:29,541 --> 00:28:31,501
I thought everything had changed.

401
00:28:32,211 --> 00:28:33,921
(I can't believe what I'm hearing.)

402
00:28:34,796 --> 00:28:36,673
My circumstances might have improved.

403
00:28:38,133 --> 00:28:41,011
But in reality, nothing has changed.

404
00:28:47,935 --> 00:28:49,061
I was still

405
00:28:50,145 --> 00:28:51,647
a nobody.

406
00:29:16,380 --> 00:29:17,964
I JUST ARRIVED IN BUSAN, MOM

407
00:29:17,965 --> 00:29:19,341
I'M MEETING SOMEONE FIRST
SEE YOU LATER

408
00:29:23,470 --> 00:29:25,681
THE X-COORDINATE OF A EQUALS ALPHA...

409
00:29:45,742 --> 00:29:47,952
Multiply both sides by 4x.

410
00:29:47,953 --> 00:29:49,997
Uncle, when did you get here?

411
00:29:50,622 --> 00:29:51,623
A long time ago.

412
00:29:51,957 --> 00:29:53,541
You're joking.

413
00:29:53,542 --> 00:29:54,793
I was watching to see
when you'd come.

414
00:29:55,252 --> 00:29:57,712
You're studying here
when you don't even study at school?

415
00:29:57,713 --> 00:30:00,673
I study whenever and wherever I can.

416
00:30:00,674 --> 00:30:03,343
- You just don't know me.
- You and your nonsense.

417
00:30:04,052 --> 00:30:06,762
- Wait up.
- Should we eat something?

418
00:30:06,763 --> 00:30:08,764
Will you buy me what I want?

419
00:30:08,765 --> 00:30:10,517
Name it first. I'll think about it.

420
00:30:11,101 --> 00:30:12,477
I want something expensive.

421
00:30:15,188 --> 00:30:17,523
You said you'd buy me what I wanted.

422
00:30:17,524 --> 00:30:18,775
I didn't say that.

423
00:30:19,192 --> 00:30:20,693
Then why did you even ask?

424
00:30:20,694 --> 00:30:22,070
To eat anything but that.

425
00:30:22,946 --> 00:30:24,947
Jeez, I should order some soju.

426
00:30:24,948 --> 00:30:26,074
Do you want a shot?

427
00:30:26,825 --> 00:30:28,534
You're a horrible uncle.

428
00:30:28,535 --> 00:30:30,037
I used to drink at your age.

429
00:30:30,704 --> 00:30:32,663
These days,
only delinquents drink at my age.

430
00:30:32,664 --> 00:30:35,125
I'm only half a delinquent,
so I can't drink.

431
00:30:35,959 --> 00:30:38,294
Eat up. Food in Seoul
isn't that special, either.

432
00:30:38,295 --> 00:30:40,088
Who eats this these days?

433
00:30:40,756 --> 00:30:43,008
I wanted something
from a famous chain.

434
00:30:46,803 --> 00:30:47,971
What's this?

435
00:30:51,808 --> 00:30:53,225
Isn't this a luxury brand?

436
00:30:53,226 --> 00:30:55,228
- You know it?
- Of course, I do.

437
00:30:55,645 --> 00:30:57,480
The celebs carry this stuff.

438
00:30:57,481 --> 00:30:59,524
I heard teenagers like it too.

439
00:31:00,317 --> 00:31:01,318
Is it for me?

440
00:31:04,321 --> 00:31:07,741
Uncle, is this how much
you care about me?

441
00:31:08,033 --> 00:31:10,369
The food will taste
much better now, won't it?

442
00:31:10,744 --> 00:31:11,745
Yeah.

443
00:31:18,460 --> 00:31:20,337
You can't post about it, okay?

444
00:31:20,754 --> 00:31:23,173
I won't. It'll get stolen
if I take it to school.

445
00:31:24,091 --> 00:31:26,301
Do you get beaten up and stuff?

446
00:31:26,968 --> 00:31:28,178
I don't.

447
00:31:28,553 --> 00:31:30,930
You need to tell me right away
if you do.

448
00:31:30,931 --> 00:31:32,891
I hope you don't get
beaten up yourself.

449
00:31:35,727 --> 00:31:36,728
The bus is here.

450
00:31:37,521 --> 00:31:38,896
I'll go ahead.

451
00:31:38,897 --> 00:31:41,232
Get a coffee somewhere
and take your time.

452
00:31:41,233 --> 00:31:42,316
What?

453
00:31:42,317 --> 00:31:44,486
You told me to meet you
so you could stay out late.

454
00:31:45,195 --> 00:31:47,863
- Well...
- Try living with my dad.

455
00:31:47,864 --> 00:31:49,074
You grow up really quickly.

456
00:31:49,658 --> 00:31:50,951
Come home before dinner.

457
00:32:52,596 --> 00:32:54,347
DONGRAE ALTERATIONS

458
00:33:10,655 --> 00:33:11,656
You're here.

459
00:33:12,908 --> 00:33:14,326
Yes, I'm here, Dad.

460
00:33:14,701 --> 00:33:15,702
THE NEW TESTAMENT

461
00:33:16,453 --> 00:33:18,413
Go upstairs.
Your mom's waiting for you.

462
00:33:18,914 --> 00:33:19,915
Okay.

463
00:33:20,957 --> 00:33:21,958
Wait.

464
00:33:22,667 --> 00:33:24,503
Your belt buckle's a little loose.

465
00:33:25,212 --> 00:33:26,421
Give it to me.

466
00:33:27,964 --> 00:33:29,381
It looks fine to me.

467
00:33:29,382 --> 00:33:30,884
It's not. Hand it over.

468
00:33:42,521 --> 00:33:43,522
Go up now.

469
00:33:44,189 --> 00:33:46,441
Okay, see you there.

470
00:33:59,704 --> 00:34:01,497
You prepare way too much food.

471
00:34:01,498 --> 00:34:03,290
- We'll never...
- I'll pack some for Eun-tae.

472
00:34:03,291 --> 00:34:05,834
We should have plenty
for Eun-seok too.

473
00:34:05,835 --> 00:34:08,462
It's too much food, even for that.

474
00:34:08,463 --> 00:34:10,422
Mom, I'm home.

475
00:34:10,423 --> 00:34:12,925
Oh, my gosh. Eun-tae's home.

476
00:34:12,926 --> 00:34:15,094
- Hello, Eun-tae.
- How are you?

477
00:34:15,095 --> 00:34:17,513
You should've come home earlier.

478
00:34:17,514 --> 00:34:19,266
My dear boy...

479
00:34:19,849 --> 00:34:21,350
- You look dreadful.
- What?

480
00:34:21,351 --> 00:34:23,270
Have you been starving yourself?

481
00:34:23,645 --> 00:34:26,146
I told you to eat on time.

482
00:34:26,147 --> 00:34:28,440
Do you still eat junk food
all the time?

483
00:34:28,441 --> 00:34:30,776
Oh, enough with the nagging, Mother.

484
00:34:30,777 --> 00:34:32,529
Give him time to breathe.

485
00:34:33,029 --> 00:34:35,657
Leave it. Berating me gives her joy.

486
00:34:36,992 --> 00:34:38,617
Hello, Uncle.

487
00:34:38,618 --> 00:34:40,369
Long time no see, A-yeong.

488
00:34:40,370 --> 00:34:42,247
You made the long trip to Busan.

489
00:34:43,623 --> 00:34:44,999
Too bad, though.

490
00:34:45,000 --> 00:34:46,918
- The delay was for nothing.
- What?

491
00:34:47,210 --> 00:34:48,420
Are you here, Eun-tae?

492
00:34:53,341 --> 00:34:54,718
Why did you come so late?

493
00:34:55,302 --> 00:34:56,760
Didn't you go to work?

494
00:34:56,761 --> 00:35:00,140
No, I heard you'd visit,
so I swapped shifts.

495
00:35:00,390 --> 00:35:01,932
Go wash your hands. Let's eat.

496
00:35:01,933 --> 00:35:03,768
Anything good for dinner, Mom?

497
00:35:04,102 --> 00:35:05,227
Let's see.

498
00:35:05,228 --> 00:35:06,562
Oh, you made skewers.

499
00:35:06,563 --> 00:35:07,897
Gosh, it's hot.

500
00:35:08,690 --> 00:35:10,525
You didn't even wash your hands.

501
00:35:11,484 --> 00:35:14,321
So how are things at work?

502
00:35:17,073 --> 00:35:18,700
Why would you ask about work?

503
00:35:19,492 --> 00:35:22,454
Why not? Can't I ask
my little brother about his job?

504
00:35:23,246 --> 00:35:26,541
I know you don't care about it.
Get to the point.

505
00:35:28,752 --> 00:35:32,047
Can you promise me one thing first?

506
00:35:32,964 --> 00:35:36,384
Don't get annoyed
and hear me out first.

507
00:35:37,594 --> 00:35:40,138
Why should I have to promise that?
Just talk.

508
00:35:46,019 --> 00:35:47,062
Take a look at this.

509
00:35:50,315 --> 00:35:55,195
It's a door hinge that prevents
people from getting hurt.

510
00:35:55,570 --> 00:35:57,946
There's a huge demand for it.

511
00:35:57,947 --> 00:36:00,909
It's going into almost
every new apartment.

512
00:36:01,451 --> 00:36:04,746
A surprising number of people
get hurt in door hinges.

513
00:36:05,955 --> 00:36:07,040
It looks pretty good.

514
00:36:08,208 --> 00:36:09,918
There's this guy who makes these.

515
00:36:10,585 --> 00:36:13,295
The deals are secured

516
00:36:13,296 --> 00:36:17,050
but he doesn't have the money
to keep the factory going.

517
00:36:17,592 --> 00:36:20,887
He says he needs
about 100 million won.

518
00:36:22,222 --> 00:36:23,431
I plan to invest.

519
00:36:24,724 --> 00:36:25,934
With what money?

520
00:36:26,351 --> 00:36:28,603
That's why I'm talking to you.

521
00:36:32,190 --> 00:36:33,191
Could you

522
00:36:34,818 --> 00:36:37,320
get me 100 million won?

523
00:36:41,950 --> 00:36:42,951
Eun-seok.

524
00:36:45,495 --> 00:36:48,915
You said some guy made that already.

525
00:36:49,666 --> 00:36:51,751
If he signed deals,
there would be sales.

526
00:36:52,085 --> 00:36:55,713
A bank would loan him the money
if he had signed contracts.

527
00:36:55,714 --> 00:36:59,426
Getting a loan is like broadcasting
he doesn't have the money.

528
00:37:00,301 --> 00:37:02,846
I've known him since I started
my own businesses.

529
00:37:03,513 --> 00:37:06,349
He can be trusted, okay?

530
00:37:07,225 --> 00:37:08,685
Even so.

531
00:37:09,269 --> 00:37:12,271
- That's a lot of money.
- I know that

532
00:37:12,272 --> 00:37:15,275
you don't have
100 million in cash right now.

533
00:37:17,986 --> 00:37:18,987
Don't you think

534
00:37:19,946 --> 00:37:23,283
you could get a loan somehow?

535
00:37:28,872 --> 00:37:30,498
You want me to take out a loan?

536
00:37:31,499 --> 00:37:32,500
Eun-tae.

537
00:37:33,334 --> 00:37:35,711
I know I got myself
into a lot of trouble so far.

538
00:37:35,712 --> 00:37:38,506
- How can you say that?
- Hear me out, will you?

539
00:37:38,798 --> 00:37:41,426
- I have a hunch.
- Will you stop it?

540
00:37:45,513 --> 00:37:46,681
It's a holiday.

541
00:37:47,891 --> 00:37:49,142
Do you know I stayed out late

542
00:37:50,018 --> 00:37:51,436
just so I could avoid
coming home to you?

543
00:37:53,688 --> 00:37:55,982
I did that because I knew
you'd be ashamed to see me.

544
00:37:58,651 --> 00:38:01,988
But the first thing you do
is ask me for money?

545
00:38:02,906 --> 00:38:03,990
Come on.

546
00:38:04,908 --> 00:38:06,242
How can you do this to me?

547
00:38:08,661 --> 00:38:09,662
Please.

548
00:38:11,122 --> 00:38:12,332
Will you grow up?

549
00:38:13,750 --> 00:38:15,084
I beg of you.

550
00:38:22,383 --> 00:38:24,260
Did you really come late to avoid me?

551
00:38:31,142 --> 00:38:32,227
I didn't know that.

552
00:38:34,395 --> 00:38:35,438
It's just that...

553
00:38:37,816 --> 00:38:39,734
I really thought
this was a good idea.

554
00:38:43,947 --> 00:38:44,989
Sorry, man.

555
00:38:46,282 --> 00:38:47,742
Pretend I didn't say a thing.

556
00:38:52,539 --> 00:38:53,748
I'm going downstairs.

557
00:38:55,416 --> 00:38:56,417
Take your time.

558
00:40:52,158 --> 00:40:57,080
THE ORDINARY JACKPOT

559
00:41:14,180 --> 00:41:15,932
ROOF TILE PRAYERS
10,000 PER TILE

560
00:41:22,563 --> 00:41:23,855
My dear son...

561
00:41:23,856 --> 00:41:26,275
MY DEAR SON

562
00:41:27,694 --> 00:41:29,362
May he grow up to be

563
00:41:30,697 --> 00:41:33,782
a decent human being.

564
00:41:33,783 --> 00:41:35,743
GROW UP TO BE A DECENT HUMAN BEING

565
00:41:39,080 --> 00:41:40,748
My dear Eun-tae...

566
00:41:42,041 --> 00:41:44,543
May he meet a good life partner...

567
00:41:44,544 --> 00:41:47,170
MAY HE MEET A GOOD LIFE PARTNER

568
00:41:47,171 --> 00:41:51,843
...and get married one day.

569
00:43:11,339 --> 00:43:13,216
Excuse me, Venerable Sir.

570
00:43:13,841 --> 00:43:16,302
I took a break to stretch and relax.

571
00:43:17,053 --> 00:43:21,057
Does that mean I have to start over?

572
00:43:21,849 --> 00:43:23,392
You can keep going.

573
00:43:24,018 --> 00:43:25,144
Okay, thank you.

574
00:43:35,113 --> 00:43:37,240
MY DEAR SON...
MY DEAR EUN-TAE...

575
00:43:38,866 --> 00:43:40,868
MY DEAR SEON-HYUK...

576
00:43:42,995 --> 00:43:45,248
MAY HIS BUSINESS FLOURISH
ONE WAY OR ANOTHER

577
00:46:18,901 --> 00:46:20,861
Subtitles by Jennifer Jean Lim
